EPILOGUE: Level complete. / EPILOGUE / The Last Thaw / For this journey / The archive ends where the water did, at the sea below the Upper Vell, on a calm grey morning with ice in the fjord. I have read your nine runs through again, start to finish, the way Tomas read his stakes: slowly, twice, not liking some of the numbers and liking others more than I expected. / The Gorge bridge stood in your run, and I have put it at the top of the list, as Callum asked. Below it runs the long column of what fell, in the order you came down the mountains. I have read it through twice. I have not crossed anything out, and I have not added anything to make it come out even. / The people are the part I am surest of. Kessel's dam went, as the 2024 report said it would, and Kessel had already gone down the valley, the last car at 07:35 with the keeper's log on the passenger seat. Everyone on every list is accounted for. They are mostly in Carran, writing to the council, which is how I know they are fine. / I am not going to tell you what it means; you were there. I will tell you what Tomas wrote inside the cover of his last notebook, under fifty-two years of numbers, in a hand that was getting larger: You cannot undo the river behind you. You can still decide where it goes next. Then he drew a kettle. / From the archive · authored for this outcome / The agents' reflection is not shown (the request failed); this one was written in advance. / OPEN THE ARCHIVE / CHAPTERS / BACK TO THE RECORD
